From 6b2c8d1e0f9a7c5b4d3e2f1a0b9c8d7e6f5a4b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: remove the other loaded hostapd ifaces before the main
 iface on a radio re-add

wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() implements the "re-add radio config"
fallback (SECDMN_ACTION_OK_NEED_RE_ADD in src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c,
taken by s_doRemoveLink() whenever hostapd does not offer LINK_REMOVE
and by s_removeBss() when the target is the main VAP) with a single
global "REMOVE <main VAP socket name>", after which
wld_rad_hostapd_addConf() re-adds the radio config listing every enabled
VAP of the radio.

That assumes all VAPs of the radio are BSSes of the main VAP's
hostapd_iface, so that the one REMOVE tears down the whole radio. With
hostapd 2024.09 ("AP MLD: Allow new link to be added through control
interface") this no longer holds for AP MLD links: in
hostapd_interface_init_bss() (src/ap/hostapd.c) an "ADD bss_config="
whose BSS has mld_ap=1 always gets a hostapd_iface of its own, even when
an iface with the same phy label exists. Since pWHM warm-adds each VAP
with its own per-BSS config (s_doAddLink() -> wld_ap_hostapd_addBssConf()),
a 6 GHz radio hosting wlan0.1 (link of MLD wlan2.1), wlan0.2 (link of
MLD wlan2.2) and wlan0.3 ends up as three hostapd_ifaces with phy label
"wlan0".

Observed on a mac80211 AP MLD setup (three MLDs across three radios)
during Freedom 100-pwhm_step_2.t, first step AccessPoint.9.Enable=0
(wlan0.3, non-Tx BSS):

  wlan0.3: disabling non Tx BSS, scheduling re-add link of Tx bss wlan0.1
  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan2.1_link2'          <- wlan0.1's iface only
  hostapd: wlan2.1_link2: interface state ENABLED->DISABLED  (one BSS)
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf (phy wlan0)  (no "new PHY")
  hostapd: wlan2.1: interface state UNINITIALIZED->COUNTRY_UPDATE
  hostapd: MLD: Failed to add link 3 in MLD wlan2.2
  hostapd: Interface initialization failed

wlan0.2's hostapd_iface (socket wlan2.2_link2) and its kernel link 2 on
netdev wlan2.2 stay registered; the re-added radio config carries wlan0.2
again with the same bssid, hostapd allocates MLD link id 3 for it and the
kernel refuses NL80211_CMD_ADD_LINK (mac80211
ieee80211_check_dup_link_addrs(), duplicate link address on the same
netdev: -EALREADY by source, hostapd logs the errno only at MSG_DEBUG).
AccessPoint.9 never reports Disabled ("enable=0 timed out"). The next
step (AccessPoint.8.Enable=0, 5 GHz) repeats it with "Failed to add link
4 in MLD wlan2.2" because wlan1.2's iface is alive too, that ADD fails
synchronously and s_doAddHostapd() escalates to "warm apply failed to add
iface conf => restart to recover": the whole shared hostapd is restarted.
The same trigger in 101-mlo_step_2.t passed because there the wlan0
BSSes were plain BSSes of one hostapd_iface (hostapd logged
wlan0.1/wlan0.2/wlan0.3 AP-DISABLED for the single REMOVE and "--> new
PHY" on the ADD).

Fix: before removing the main iface, remove every other VAP of the radio
that hostapd currently has loaded (its control socket exists) as the
first BSS of a hostapd_iface of its own, with the recipe already used
for the main iface: "SET interface <sockname>" on the BSS socket when
the socket name is not the bare ifname (MLD link sockets are
"<iface>_link<N>", and hostapd_remove_iface() matches the configured
interface name of bss[0]), then the global "REMOVE <sockname>", which
runs the whole-iface teardown and thereby removes the kernel MLD link
(hostapd_cleanup_driver() -> hostapd_if_link_remove()).

A VAP that is a secondary BSS of a hostapd_iface owned by another VAP of
the radio is deliberately left alone. This is the layout after the first
re-add: the full radio config goes in as one "ADD bss_config=", so the
main VAP is bss[0] and the other MLD links are bss[1..] of one iface.
Addressing such a BSS with the recipe above is wrong because hostapd's
"SET interface" rewrites the interface name of bss[0] of the iface
holding the addressed BSS, exactly like the "interface=" config line
(hostapd_config_fill(), hostapd/config_file.c: os_strlcpy(
conf->bss[0]->iface, ...)), not the name of the addressed BSS. The
second non-Tx BSS disable of the test (AccessPoint.6.Enable=0, wlan0.2)
showed it with a first version of this change that removed every loaded
VAP:

  wlan0.2: disabling non Tx BSS, scheduling re-add link of Tx bss wlan0.1
  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan2.2_link3'    <- the main VAP wlan0.1, renamed
  hostapd: wlan2.2_link3: interface state ENABLED->DISABLED
  hostapd: wlan2.2: AP-DISABLED                <- bss[1] = wlan0.2
  hostapd: wlan2.2_link3: AP-DISABLED          <- bss[0] = wlan0.1
  wld: wlan0: fail to restore iface name (wlan0.1->wlan2.1_link3)
  wld: wlan0: warm apply failed to remove iface conf => restart to recover

The whole iface went away under the main VAP's feet and the main-iface
step then failed on a dead socket. Such a secondary BSS is removed by
its owner's whole-iface teardown anyway (hostapd_free_hapd_data() calls
hostapd_if_link_remove() for a started non-first MLD link BSS that is
not bss[0]), so skipping it keeps the kernel state correct.

Whether a BSS is bss[0] of its iface is read from hostapd itself: the
"STATUS" reply on any BSS socket lists the BSSes of the iface holding it
(bss[N]=/bssid[N]=, hostapd_ctrl_iface_status()), so the VAP is the
first BSS iff bssid[0] is its own BSSID. The connection socket names are
refreshed first (wld_wpaCtrlMngr_checkAllIfaces()) since a BSS socket is
renamed to its MLD link socket after setup, and the command wrapper
already uses a temporary connection when the BSS's wpactrl client is not
connected, so a loaded-but-unready BSS is handled too. A VAP whose socket
is gone is skipped as already removed. Any SET or REMOVE failure, or a
BSS whose iface membership cannot be determined, makes the function
fail, so that s_doRemoveHostapd() runs its existing recovery instead of
re-adding a config on top of a live duplicate. The main-iface removal
itself is unchanged.

pWHM v7.29.20 is the newest source available locally and the upstream
pwhm repository could not be reached from here (HTTP 403), so the
current upstream wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() was not compared.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c |  135 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 123 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
@@ -524,6 +524,80 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * @brief remove one hostapd iface, addressed by the control socket name of its first BSS
+ *
+ * hostapd's global "REMOVE <name>" tears down the whole hostapd_iface whose
+ * first BSS (bss[0]) is configured with interface name <name>
+ * (hostapd_remove_iface(), src/ap/hostapd.c), including its secondary BSSes.
+ * For an AP MLD link BSS the control socket is named "<iface>_link<N>" while
+ * the configured interface name is the MLD's netdev, shared by all its links,
+ * so the interface name is first set to the socket name to make the REMOVE
+ * target unambiguous. Note that "SET interface" always rewrites the name of
+ * bss[0] of the iface owning the addressed BSS (hostapd_config_fill(),
+ * hostapd/config_file.c, same as the "interface=" config line), which is why
+ * this helper must only be used with the first BSS of an iface.
+ * The command wrapper uses a temporary connection when the wpactrl client of
+ * the BSS is not connected, so a loaded BSS is removed even while its client
+ * is unready.
+ *
+ * @param pR radio context
+ * @param pgIface hostapd global control interface
+ * @param pIface control interface of the first BSS of the iface to remove
+ *
+ * @return SWL_RC_OK when the removing cmd is accepted.
+ *         SWL_RC_CONTINUE when the command is accepted but still being processed by hostapd
+ *         Otherwise error code (also when the interface name could not be set).
+ */
+static swl_rc_ne s_removeIfaceBySockName(T_Radio* pR, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pgIface, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface) {
+    swl_rc_ne rc;
+    const char* skname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pIface);
+    const char* ifname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getName(pIface);
+    if(!swl_str_matches(skname, ifname)) {
+        rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pIface, "OK", "SET interface %s", skname);
+        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to restore iface name (%s->%s)", pR->Name, ifname, skname);
+    }
+    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pgIface, "OK", "REMOVE %s", skname);
+    //the call may timeout while being applied, but that only happens on success
+    if(rc == SWL_RC_NOT_AVAILABLE) {
+        rc = SWL_RC_CONTINUE;
+    }
+    return rc;
+}
+
+/**
+ * @brief check whether a loaded BSS is the first BSS (bss[0]) of its hostapd iface
+ *
+ * hostapd reports on the control socket of any BSS the BSS list of the
+ * hostapd_iface holding it ("STATUS" reply lines bss[N]=/bssid[N]=,
+ * hostapd_ctrl_iface_status(), src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c). bss[0] is the BSS
+ * whose interface name the global "REMOVE" matches for the whole iface and
+ * whose interface name "SET interface" rewrites.
+ *
+ * @param pR radio context
+ * @param pAP the VAP
+ * @param pIface control interface of the VAP's BSS
+ *
+ * @return SWL_TRL_TRUE when the BSS is bss[0] of its hostapd iface
+ *         SWL_TRL_FALSE when it is a secondary BSS of an iface owned by another VAP
+ *         SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN when hostapd could not be queried
+ */
+static swl_trl_e s_isBssIfaceFirst(T_Radio* pR, T_AccessPoint* pAP, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface) {
+    ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pAP->pSSID, SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN, ME, "NULL");
+    size_t maxMsgLen = wld_wpaCtrl_getMaxMsgLen();
+    char reply[maxMsgLen];
+    memset(reply, 0, sizeof(reply));
+    swl_rc_ne rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtGetResponse(pIface, reply, sizeof(reply), "STATUS");
+    ASSERTW_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN, ME, "%s: fail to get status of bss %s", pR->Name, pAP->alias);
+    char bssid0Str[SWL_MAC_CHAR_LEN] = {0};
+    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_getInReplyParamValStr(reply, "bssid[0]", bssid0Str, sizeof(bssid0Str));
+    ASSERTW_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN, ME, "%s: no bssid[0] in status of bss %s", pR->Name, pAP->alias);
+    swl_macBin_t bssid0 = SWL_MAC_BIN_NEW();
+    ASSERTW_TRUE(swl_typeMacBin_fromChar(&bssid0, bssid0Str), SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN, ME, "%s: invalid bssid[0] (%s) of bss %s",
+                 pR->Name, bssid0Str, pAP->alias);
+    return SWL_MAC_BIN_MATCHES(&bssid0, pAP->pSSID->BSSID) ? SWL_TRL_TRUE : SWL_TRL_FALSE;
+}
+
+/**
  * @brief remove entire radio and vaps config from hostapd
  * (this will trigger removing all secondary BSSs netdev ifaces and stop radio activity)
  *
@@ -543,19 +617,56 @@
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pIface, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: hostapd has no default wpactrl iface ready", pR->Name);
     wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pgIface = wld_secDmn_getGlobalCtrlIface(pSecDmn);
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pgIface, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: hostapd has no global iface ready", pR->Name);
-    swl_rc_ne rc;
-    const char* skname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pIface);
-    const char* ifname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getName(pIface);
-    if(!swl_str_matches(skname, ifname)) {
-        rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pIface, "OK", "SET interface %s", skname);
-        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to restore main iface name (%s->%s)", pR->Name, ifname, skname);
-    }
-    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pgIface, "OK", "REMOVE %s", skname);
-    //the call may timeout while being applied, but that only happens on success
-    if(rc == SWL_RC_NOT_AVAILABLE) {
-        rc = SWL_RC_CONTINUE;
+
+    /*
+     * A secondary VAP added with its own "ADD bss_config=" as an AP MLD link
+     * (mld_ap=1) is not a BSS of the main VAP's hostapd iface: hostapd allocates
+     * a separate hostapd_iface for every such ADD (hostapd_interface_init_bss(),
+     * src/ap/hostapd.c, "AP MLD can be enabled with the same interface name").
+     * "REMOVE <main>" therefore leaves those VAPs, and their kernel MLD links,
+     * fully registered, and the radio config re-added right after (which lists
+     * every enabled VAP of the radio) duplicates them: the driver link add for
+     * the duplicate is refused by the kernel (same link address already present
+     * on the MLD netdev), hostapd reports "MLD: Failed to add link N in MLD X"
+     * and the warm re-add fails.
+     * So remove, before the main iface, every other VAP of the radio that
+     * hostapd currently has loaded (its control socket exists) as the first
+     * BSS of a hostapd iface of its own. A VAP that is a secondary BSS of an
+     * iface owned by another VAP of the radio (e.g. all VAPs of a radio config
+     * re-added as one "ADD bss_config=" get one iface, the main VAP first) is
+     * left alone: it is removed together with that iface, and addressing it
+     * directly would rename and remove the owner's iface instead (see
+     * s_removeIfaceBySockName()). A VAP whose socket is already gone (not
+     * loaded, or removed together with a previously removed iface) is skipped.
+     * Any failure aborts the removal so that the caller runs its recovery
+     * instead of re-adding a config on top of a live duplicate.
+     */
+    wld_wpaCtrlMngr_checkAllIfaces(pMgr);
+    T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
+    wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pR) {
+        wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pApIface = pAP->wpaCtrlInterface;
+        if((pApIface == NULL) || (pApIface == pIface)) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if(!wld_wpaCtrlInterface_checkConnectionPath(pApIface)) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: bss %s not loaded, skip removal", pR->Name, pAP->alias);
+            continue;
+        }
+        const char* apSkname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pApIface);
+        swl_trl_e isFirst = s_isBssIfaceFirst(pR, pAP, pApIface);
+        ASSERT_NOT_EQUALS(isFirst, SWL_TRL_UNKNOWN, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: unknown hostapd iface of bss %s (%s), abort radio removal",
+                          pR->Name, pAP->alias, apSkname);
+        if(isFirst == SWL_TRL_FALSE) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: bss %s (%s) is a secondary bss of another iface, removed with it", pR->Name, pAP->alias, apSkname);
+            continue;
+        }
+        SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: remove iface of bss %s (%s) before main iface", pR->Name, pAP->alias, apSkname);
+        swl_rc_ne apRc = s_removeIfaceBySockName(pR, pgIface, pApIface);
+        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(apRc), apRc, ME, "%s: fail to remove bss %s (%s) rc %d, abort radio removal",
+                    pR->Name, pAP->alias, apSkname, apRc);
     }
-    return rc;
+
+    return s_removeIfaceBySockName(pR, pgIface, pIface);
 }
 
 swl_trl_e wld_rad_hostapd_getCfgParamSupp(T_Radio* pRad, const char* param) {
